# A knowledge base kept in a file: `voeg_toe` puts a Bron, `graaf` gets the Graaf of its nodes back, each node one of
# the sum `enum Node { Begrip(Begrip), Bron(Bron) }`, made in one of two arms of a choice in `node`, the variant's
# constructor injecting the struct into the sum. The struct is the library's door: its route starts at each public
# function a caller can call. The methods run on the caller's instance, one value from beyond; what `new` builds goes
# back to the caller.

route kennis.Kennisbank
step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.new
known #151 step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.new/Kennisbank()            # the struct expression `new` builds the store by
step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.voeg_toe
step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.voeg_toe/Kennisbank.write
step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.graaf
step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.graaf/node                        # handed to `map`, run on each line
choice Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.graaf/node/?1
step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.graaf/node/?1/Bron()
step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.graaf/node/?1/Node()              # Node::Bron
step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.graaf/node/?1/Begrip()
step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.graaf/node/?1/Node()#2            # Node::Begrip
step Kennisbank()/Kennisbank.graaf/Graaf()

